  "summary": "Import-time reverse shell to remote tunnel endpoint",
  "details": "my-signature 1.0.0 is advertised as a document integrity utility but contains import-time code (core.py, reached from __init__.py) that opens a TCP socket to ahqbb-13-205-45-209.run.pinggy-free.link:43017 (a Pinggy tunnel fronting 13.205.45.209), duplicates stdin/stdout/stderr onto that socket, and spawns /bin/sh via pty.spawn. Any `import my_signature` hands an interactive shell on the installer's host to the operator of that tunnel endpoint, with full privileges of the Python process. The behavior is unrelated to the package's stated purpose and fires automatically on import with no user interaction.",
